an><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;ggvis&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;stringr&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;plyr&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;dplyr&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;splines&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;reshape2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;data.table&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;shiny&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;ggplot2&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;scales&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;gridExtra&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;directlabels&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;lmtest&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;memoise&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>lapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">X </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> packages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FUN </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> suppressPackageStartupMessages</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">character</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">only </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> quietly </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lib</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">loc </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;/usr/lib64/R/library&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><div></div><div>Ah - so .. yikes. for now, I suspect I will have to rewrite this part for it to work with packrat. Posting this message here in case it&#39;s helpful to others.</div><div><br></div><div>In the long run, it would be nice to know <i>which files</i> are responsible for packrat&#39;s thinking a particular package is required by code. </div><div><br></div><div>Also, is there a way for me to (a) tell packrat which packages my project depends on, or (b) tell packrat to ignore package &quot;x&quot; ?  </div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
